---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Women Safety Resources — Nexus Wave Technologies"
  description="A practical women-safety resource centre with emergency contacts, official Indian support services, digital safety guidance, legal resources, safety planning and self-defence learning."
>
  <section class="hero safety-resources-hero">
    <div class="container hero-shell">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Women Safety Resources</p>
        <h1>Know your options. Build your safety plan. Get help when you need it.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          This page brings together emergency contacts, official support services, legal and workplace resources,
          cyber-safety guidance, practical safety habits and self-defence learning in one place.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="#emergency">Emergency help</a>
          <a class="button" href="#resources">Official resources</a>
          <a class="button" href="#self-defence">Self-defence & training</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-panel emergency-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">If danger is happening now</p>
        <h2>Move toward safety first.</h2>
        <p class="muted">If you are in immediate danger in India, call <strong>112</strong>. Go toward a safer public place if you can do so safely, and ask a trusted person for help.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="tel:112">Call 112</a>
          <a class="button" href="tel:181">Women Helpline 181</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="emergency">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Emergency contacts</p>
          <h2>Keep these numbers easy to reach.</h2>
          <p class="muted">Numbers and services below are based on current official Indian government sources. Always verify local arrangements if you are travelling or living outside India.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-4">
        <article class="card resource-card emergency-card">
          <span class="resource-number">112</span>
          <h3>Emergency response</h3>
          <p class="muted">Pan-India emergency response for police, fire, medical and other urgent assistance.</p>
          <a class="button primary" href="tel:112">Call 112</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://112.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official 112 website</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card resource-card">
          <span class="resource-number">181</span>
          <h3>Women Helpline</h3>
          <p class="muted">Women can seek support, information and connections to emergency services and One Stop Centres.</p>
          <a class="button primary" href="tel:181">Call 181</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://wcd.gov.in/women/help" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official Women Helpline</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card resource-card">
          <span class="resource-number">1930</span>
          <h3>Cyber crime helpline</h3>
          <p class="muted">Use this for cyber-related incidents and especially urgent reporting of cyber financial fraud.</p>
          <a class="button primary" href="tel:1930">Call 1930</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://www.cybercrime.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cyber Crime Portal</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card resource-card">
          <span class="resource-number">1098</span>
          <h3>Child Helpline</h3>
          <p class="muted">For children who need protection or assistance. In an immediate emergency, 112 is also available.</p>
          <a class="button primary" href="tel:1098">Call 1098</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://www.spniwcd.wcd.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official WCD resources</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="callout" role="note">
        <strong>Important:</strong> Nexus is not an emergency-response service. A website report should never delay a call to emergency services when there is immediate danger.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft" id="resources">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Official support</p>
          <h2>Government and institutional resources</h2>
          <p class="muted">Use the official service for the type of help you need rather than relying only on a private platform.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">One Stop Centre</p>
          <h3>Medical, legal, police, shelter and counselling support</h3>
          <p class="muted">One Stop Centres under Mission Shakti provide integrated support for women affected by violence, including medical, legal, temporary shelter, police assistance and counselling.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://wcd.gov.in/women/one-stop-centre-header" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find official OSC information</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Free legal aid</p>
          <h3>NALSA and State Legal Services Authorities</h3>
          <p class="muted">Women can seek free legal assistance through Legal Services Authorities. NALSA also provides a national legal-aid helpline at 15100.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button" href="tel:15100">Call 15100</a>
            <a class="button" href="https://nalsa.gov.in/womens-assistance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Women & legal aid</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Shelter and longer-term support</p>
          <h3>Shakti Sadan</h3>
          <p class="muted">Shakti Sadan supports women in distress and difficult circumstances, including access to shelter, food, legal and medical services, counselling and vocational support.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://wcd.gov.in/offerings/shakti-sadan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official Shakti Sadan information</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Workplace safety</p>
          <h3>SHe-Box</h3>
          <p class="muted">For workplace sexual-harassment matters, the Ministry of Women and Child Development provides the SHe-Box system and related official information.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://shebox.wcd.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open SHe-Box</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Cyber safety</p>
          <h3>National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal</h3>
          <p class="muted">The official portal supports reporting of cyber crime, including dedicated pathways for women and children and anonymous reporting for eligible categories.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://www.cybercrime.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Report cyber crime</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Women and law</p>
          <h3>Understand the protections available to you</h3>
          <p class="muted">The Ministry lists legislation and resources covering workplace sexual harassment, domestic violence, cyber-related issues, trafficking, child protection and other areas.</p>
          <a class="button" href="https://wcd.gov.in/women/legislations" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official legislation list</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="safety-plan">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Personal safety plan</p>
          <h2>Prepare before you need it.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Choose trusted contacts</h3><p class="muted">Keep two or three trusted people who know how to reach you and what to do if you stop responding unexpectedly.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Know your exits</h3><p class="muted">At home, work, college, hotels and unfamiliar places, notice exits, reception desks, security points and public areas.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Keep essentials ready</h3><p class="muted">Keep your phone charged, emergency contacts accessible, identification and essential medicines available, and transport options in mind.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Use location sharing thoughtfully</h3><p class="muted">Share live location with a trusted person when appropriate. Review which apps and people can see your location and remove access you no longer need.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Have a code word</h3><p class="muted">A simple agreed phrase can tell a trusted person that you need help without explaining the situation publicly.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Plan a safe destination</h3><p class="muted">Identify places you can reach quickly: a trusted home, staffed public place, police facility, hospital or other safe location.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Everyday safety</p>
          <h2>Practical habits for different situations</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Walking and commuting</h3>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Prefer well-lit, populated routes when practical.</li>
            <li>Keep enough phone battery for navigation and emergency calls.</li>
            <li>When something feels unsafe, move toward people, staff, security or an open business instead of confronting the person alone.</li>
            <li>For late travel, tell a trusted person your expected arrival time and update them if plans change.</li>
            <li>If a vehicle or person appears to be following you, do not lead them directly to your home; move toward a busy, staffed place and ask for help.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Cab, auto and public transport</h3>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Check the vehicle and driver details before entering where the service provides them.</li>
            <li>Use official booking apps or trusted transport services where possible.</li>
            <li>Share trip details with someone you trust when appropriate.</li>
            <li>If uncomfortable, ask to stop at a populated, staffed location rather than an isolated point.</li>
            <li>In immediate danger, prioritize getting help and contacting 112 rather than arguing with the driver.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Online and social media</h3>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Use unique passwords and multi-factor authentication where available.</li>
            <li>Do not share OTPs, recovery codes, banking PINs or passwords with anyone.</li>
            <li>Review privacy settings for location, photos, contacts and story visibility.</li>
            <li>Be careful with unknown links, QR codes, remote-access requests and urgent payment requests.</li>
            <li>For threats, impersonation, intimate-image abuse or other cyber crime, preserve relevant evidence and consider the official Cyber Crime Reporting Portal.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Home and relationship safety</h3>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Abuse can be physical, sexual, emotional, psychological, economic or digital. You do not have to wait for physical violence before seeking support.</li>
            <li>If leaving could increase danger, plan discreetly and seek professional or trusted support rather than announcing the plan to the abusive person.</li>
            <li>Keep copies of important documents and essential contacts somewhere safe if doing so does not create additional risk.</li>
            <li>For immediate danger, prioritize emergency help and a safe place.</li>
            <li>One Stop Centres and Women Helpline 181 can help connect women to appropriate support.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="digital-safety">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Digital safety checklist</p>
          <h2>Protect your accounts, identity and evidence.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-4">
        <article class="card"><h3>Account security</h3><p class="muted">Use a strong, unique password and MFA. Review active sessions and recovery methods regularly.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Phone security</h3><p class="muted">Use a screen lock, keep the operating system updated, and avoid giving unknown apps accessibility or device-control permissions.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Privacy review</h3><p class="muted">Check app permissions, location sharing, Bluetooth visibility, cloud sharing and social-media audience settings.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Evidence</h3><p class="muted">When safe to do so, keep original messages, URLs, usernames, dates, transaction references and screenshots. Do not put yourself in danger to collect evidence.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft" id="self-defence">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Self-defence & confidence</p>
          <h2>Learn skills that help you create distance and get away.</h2>
          <p class="muted">Self-defence is not about proving strength or winning a fight. The main objective is to recognize danger, create an opportunity to escape and reach help.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Train regularly</h3>
          <p class="muted">Consider a reputable self-defence, martial-arts or personal-safety class. Look for qualified instructors, a safe training environment and practical scenario-based training.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Useful skills to practise</h3>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Awareness and early-risk recognition</li>
            <li>Strong verbal boundaries and confident communication</li>
            <li>Breaking contact and creating distance</li>
            <li>Safe movement toward exits and populated areas</li>
            <li>Calling for help clearly and quickly</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Martial arts can help</h3>
          <p class="muted">Boxing, kickboxing, judo, karate, taekwondo, Brazilian jiu-jitsu and other disciplines can develop coordination, conditioning, confidence and controlled practice. Choose based on the instructor, safety standards and training goals rather than the name of the style alone.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Remember:</strong> no technique guarantees safety. If escape is possible, escaping and getting to other people is usually the priority. Do not stay in a dangerous situation just to use a technique you have learned.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">If something happens</p>
        <h2>You do not have to handle everything alone.</h2>
        <ol class="feature-list">
          <li>Get to a safer place if you can do so safely.</li>
          <li>Call 112 for immediate danger.</li>
          <li>Contact 181 for women-focused support and referrals.</li>
          <li>For cyber incidents, use the official Cyber Crime Reporting Portal and 1930 where applicable.</li>
          <li>For legal assistance, contact NALSA or the relevant State/District Legal Services Authority.</li>
          <li>Seek medical care when needed and consider asking a trusted person to stay with you.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">What not to do</p>
        <h2>Safety comes before confrontation.</h2>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Do not confront a dangerous person just to collect evidence.</li>
          <li>Do not share your OTP, banking PIN, password or recovery code with someone claiming to help.</li>
          <li>Do not meet an online stranger alone because they are pressuring you to do so.</li>
          <li>Do not assume you caused or deserved abuse because you were unable to prevent it.</li>
          <li>Do not rely on a website or app as a substitute for emergency services.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft">
    <div class="container card future-safety-game">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coming later</p>
      <h2>Learn safety through practice.</h2>
      <p class="muted">Nexus can later turn this resource into an interactive safety-learning game with scenario-based decisions, awareness exercises, escape planning, digital-safety challenges, emergency-call practice and self-defence learning. The goal will be education and confidence—not real-world confrontation.</p>
      <p class="note">The game should be designed with qualified safety educators and accessibility testing before it is presented as a learning resource.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Official sources</p>
          <h2>Verify important information directly</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="source-list">
        <a href="https://112.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>112.gov.in</strong><span>Emergency Response Support System</span></a>
        <a href="https://wcd.gov.in/women/help" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Women Helpline 181</strong><span>Ministry of Women and Child Development</span></a>
        <a href="https://wcd.gov.in/women/one-stop-centre-header" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>One Stop Centres</strong><span>Integrated support for women affected by violence</span></a>
        <a href="https://wcd.gov.in/offerings/shakti-sadan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Shakti Sadan</strong><span>Shelter and support for women in distress</span></a>
        <a href="https://www.cybercrime.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal</strong><span>Cyber crime reporting and tracking</span></a>
        <a href="https://nalsa.gov.in/womens-assistance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>NALSA Women Assistance</strong><span>Free legal aid and legal guidance</span></a>
        <a href="https://shebox.wcd.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>SHe-Box</strong><span>Workplace sexual-harassment complaint platform</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .safety-resources-hero{padding-bottom:48px}
  .emergency-panel{border-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-danger) 35%,var(--color-border));background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-danger) 5%,var(--color-surface))}
  .resource-card{display:grid;align-content:start;gap:10px}
  .resource-number{font-size:2rem;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:-.04em;color:var(--color-primary)}
  .resource-card .button{margin-top:6px}
  .text-link{font-size:.9rem;font-weight:700}
  .callout{margin-top:20px;padding:18px 20px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-left:4px solid var(--color-primary);border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.65}
  .future-safety-game{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--color-surface-accent),var(--color-surface-raised))}
  .source-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px}
  .source-list a{display:grid;gap:3px;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:var(--color-surface);text-decoration:none;color:var(--color-text)}
  .source-list a:hover{border-color:var(--color-border-strong);background:var(--color-surface-soft)}
  .source-list span{color:var(--color-text-muted);font-size:.9rem}
  @media(max-width:850px){.source-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
